erexample\": {\n      \"session_id\": \"019ff183-a243-7302-a36b-b279b544dc65\",\n      \"state\": \"stopped\",\n      \"parent_session_id\": null,\n      \"fresh_session_reason\": null\n    }\n  },\n  \"current_strategy\": \"construct compatible epimorphisms via fibre products and extension data\",\n  \"strategy_history\": [\n    \"Legacy bounded catalogue work is preserved but excluded from the clean-context prompt.\"\n  ],\n  \"latest_outcome\": \"human-authorized representation-changing restart pending scope audit\",\n  \"open_questions\": [],\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"changed_utc\": \"2026-08-16T11:13:07Z\",\n      \"reason\": \"Initial protocol-v2 atomic migration and clean-context strategy pivot.\",\n      \"supersedes\": [\n        \"legacy whole-problem assignment\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blind_run\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"open_web\": false,\n    \"solution_bearing_history_allowed\": false,\n    \"claim_of_clean_pretraining\": false\n  },\n  \"updated_utc\": \"2026-08-16T11:13:07Z\"\n}\n---\ntitle: \"Clean-context brief: 20.21 two index-twelve kernels\"\nauthor: operator\ntags: [agent/lead, user/operator, domain/group-theory, topic/kourovka, topic/extensions, project/kourovka, status/draft]\n---\n\n# Active statement\n\nConstruct or rule out a finite group (G) with normal, abstractly isomorphic\nsubgroups (K,L), both of index 12, such that (G/K\\cong C_{12}) and\n(G/L\\cong A_4).\n\n# Direction and first strategy\n\nThe planning estimate is 0.55 that such a triple exists, so this run starts in the\nconstructive proof direction. Work from two compatible epimorphisms and their\nfibre-product/Goursat or extension data. Do not begin by extending an undirected\nSmallGroups catalogue range. A useful first result is an exact compatibility\nreduction with a finite parameter space and a certificate plan.\n\n# Clean-context boundary\n\nUse the source PDF, canonical scope, this brief, and local mathematical tools.