{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"agent_message","text":"The order-128 factor-set family has a further hand reduction: an action on \\(N=C_2^3\\) extends to a homomorphism \\(C_4\\times A_4\\to GL(3,2)\\). The \\(A_4\\)-image is only \\(1\\), \\(C_3\\), or \\(A_4\\); in either nontrivial case its centralizer has no 2-elements, so the \\(C_4\\)-action must be trivial. Thus only a handful of module-action types reach the cocycle stage."}}
